  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 345 AM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nUnfortunately, the aforementioned shortwave will drop a dry cold \nfront into the area Saturday night, w/latest NAM/GFS soundings \npegging fropa at KMAF at around 05Z Saturday.  This will send \ntemperatures plunging Sunday, to ~ 8-10 F below normal, 15-20 F \ncooler than Saturday. \n\nHowever, this cold snap will be quite ephemeral, as surface winds \nquickly veer back to return flow late Sunday afternoon as zonal flow \naloft develops in the wake of the exiting shortwave.  Highs make a \nrespectable recovery Monday, back into the 70s most locations. \nTuesday, an upper trough is forecast to make landfall on the west \ncoast just south of the Bay Area, transitioning zonal flow aloft \nover the area to southwest.  Thicknesses will continue increasing, \nadding another 2-3 F to Monday's highs.\n\nWednesday, the west coast trough is forecast to open, traversing to \nthe Four Corners by 00Z Thursday.  Increasingly southwest flow aloft \nand large-scale ascent ahead of this feature will open a short \nwindow Wednesday afternoon/night for a chance of showers, which \nlooks to be our only chance for precipitation this forecast.\n\nThursday, the trough pushes east of the region, dragging a sort of \nPac front through the area and closing out the long-term forecast \nwith highs a degree or two below normal, putting most locations in \nthe 50s and 60s.",
